WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.173
Let's build a quantity break with MultiTier Discounts,
using our Fieldnote demo store.

2
00:00:05.523 --> 00:00:12.337
The Cobalt notebook costs eighteen dollars. Two units
receive ten percent off. Three or more receive fifteen

3
00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:13.139
percent off.

4
00:00:13.489 --> 00:00:19.676
We'll review the setup, then check the product widget,
cart and actual checkout. We won't place an order.

5
00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:25.357
From All Campaigns, choose Create New Campaign, then
the Quantity breaks starter.

6
00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:31.893
Give the offer a clear name. Use Automatic execution
and a percentage discount for this example.

7
00:00:32.243 --> 00:00:39.463
A recipe only fills in starting values. It doesn't
save or activate a campaign, so review every step

8
00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:40.265
before publishing.

9
00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:46.583
In Conditions, choose Quantity Breaks and select only
the Cobalt notebook in Products.

10
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:53.687
Confirm the picker and wait for the selected product
summary. Leaving this optional filter empty would make

11
00:00:53.687 --> 00:00:54.879
the offer broader.

12
00:00:55.229 --> 00:01:01.294
Quantity breaks evaluate each qualifying cart line
separately. Two different products with one unit each

13
00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.719
do not make a two-unit line.

14
00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:10.095
Use a price-position offer instead when you want
separate rewards on the second and third product.

15
00:01:11.145 --> 00:01:16.456
In Rewards, set the first minimum quantity to two and
its discount to ten percent.

16
00:01:16.806 --> 00:01:23.077
Set the next minimum to three and its discount to
fifteen percent. Remove unused recipe tiers.

17
00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:29.637
These numbers are quantity thresholds, not product
positions. The highest matching tier wins; ten and

18
00:01:29.637 --> 00:01:32.120
fifteen percent are not added together.

19
00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:38.553
At three units, all three notebooks receive the
fifteen-percent rate when discounted quantity is

20
00:01:38.553 --> 00:01:38.988
unlimited.

21
00:01:40.038 --> 00:01:46.020
In Review and launch, check the selected product, both
tiers, schedule and combination settings.

22
00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:53.352
In Quantity and Sorting, zero means unlimited
discounted units per line. Keep the test free of other

23
00:01:53.352 --> 00:01:53.762
discounts.

24
00:01:54.112 --> 00:02:00.031
Save as an inactive draft, then reopen it to confirm
the selection and tier values persisted.

25
00:02:00.381 --> 00:02:06.737
Our new draft stays inactive. The storefront
demonstration uses the existing identical demo offer,

26
00:02:06.737 --> 00:02:09.915
so we don't enable two overlapping campaigns.

27
00:02:10.965 --> 00:02:17.374
Open the Cobalt product in the demo theme. Quantity
Tiers shows the offer beside the purchase controls.

28
00:02:17.724 --> 00:02:23.579
One unit is eighteen dollars. At two units, the total
is thirty-two dollars and forty cents.

29
00:02:23.929 --> 00:02:30.601
Choose three units. Fifteen percent off fifty-four
dollars saves eight dollars and ten cents, leaving

30
00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.824
forty-five dollars and ninety cents.

31
00:02:33.174 --> 00:02:39.581
The widget explains the offer, but the cart and
checkout must confirm the real result. Add three

32
00:02:39.581 --> 00:02:39.958
notebooks.

33
00:02:41.008 --> 00:02:47.443
In the cart, confirm three Cobalt notebooks, eight
dollars and ten cents saved, and forty-five dollars

34
00:02:47.443 --> 00:02:49.454
and ninety cents in merchandise.

35
00:02:49.804 --> 00:02:55.680
Continue to checkout and compare the same product,
quantity, discount and merchandise amount.

36
00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:02.880
Tax and delivery may be separate. Opening checkout is
a test, not a completed order. Don't enter payment

37
00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.402
details for this walkthrough.

38
00:03:05.452 --> 00:03:11.362
Return to the cart and reduce the qualifying line to
one. Its quantity discount should disappear.

39
00:03:11.712 --> 00:03:18.189
Remove the notebook and test the Coral product outside
the selected scope. This offer must not discount

40
00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:18.570
Coral.

41
00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:25.844
Finish with an empty test cart. Your own launch checks
should also cover four units, split lines, mobile, and

42
00:03:25.844 --> 00:03:28.759
any codes or markets you intend to support.

43
00:03:29.109 --> 00:03:35.691
Use the written quantity-break guide to repeat these
checks. Only activate your own offer once its real

44
00:03:35.691 --> 00:03:38.014
cart and checkout match the promise.
